valuation>N</evaluation><unconditional>N</unconditional></hop><hop><from>02 Load dimensions (SCD2)</from><to>Mark run failed</to><from_nr>0</from_nr><to_nr>0</to_nr><enabled>Y</enabled><evaluation>N</evaluation><unconditional>N</unconditional></hop><hop><from>03 Load fact tables</from><to>Mark run failed</to><from_nr>0</from_nr><to_nr>0</to_nr><enabled>Y</enabled><evaluation>N</evaluation><unconditional>N</unconditional></hop><hop><from>04 Data quality checks</from><to>Mark run failed</to><from_nr>0</from_nr><to_nr>0</to_nr><enabled>Y</enabled><evaluation>N</evaluation><unconditional>N</unconditional></hop><hop><from>05 Revenue reconciliation</from><to>Mark run failed</to><from_nr>0</from_nr><to_nr>0</to_nr><enabled>Y</enabled><evaluation>N</evaluation><unconditional>N</unconditional></hop><hop><from>Mark run failed</from><to>Abort</to><from_nr>0</from_nr><to_nr>0</to_nr><enabled>Y</enabled><evaluation>Y</evaluation><unconditional>Y</unconditional></hop></hops>
<notepads><notepad><note>RetailFlow Master Pipeline (Pentaho engine)
Same 5 stages as the web app runner: Extract -&gt; Load dimensions (SCD2) -&gt; Load facts -&gt; Data quality -&gt; Reconcile.
Run is logged to ops.etl_run_log (engine = pentaho, trigger = pentaho) + ops.etl_stage_log, so it appears on the Runs / Monitoring pages.
Red hops = failure path: run marked failed, job aborts.</note><xloc>48</xloc><yloc>24</yloc><width>1100</width><heigth>96</heigth><fontname>Segoe UI</fontname><fontsize>9</fontsize><fontbold>N</fontbold><fontitalic>N</fontitalic><fontcolorred>14</fontcolorred><fontcolorgreen>13</fontcolorgreen><fontcolorblue>15</fontcolorblue><backgroundcolorred>254</backgroundcolorred><backgroundcolorgreen>208</backgroundcolorgreen><backgroundcolorblue>26</backgroundcolorblue><bordercolorred>14</bordercolorred><bordercolorgreen>13</bordercolorgreen><bordercolorblue>15</bordercolorblue><drawshadow>Y</drawshadow></notepad></notepads><attributes/></job>
